\label{thm:seb_coll}
    There is a function $H$ on $S(p,q,r)$, $H:S(p,q,r)\to[0,1],$ that is Morse away from the orbifold points,  such that
    \begin{itemize}
        \item it has unique maxima $y$,
        \item it has minima exactly at the orbifold points $\{v_{ij}\}$, $i\in \{ 1,2,\dots,s_j\}$ \item near the orbifold points $H$ is modeled by $|\phi|^2$ for certain automorphic forms $\phi$ on $\mathbb{H} \times \widetilde {\mathbb{C}^\times}$.
    \end{itemize}
    Let $x_1,\dots , x_r$ denote the critical points of index one. For every $T>0$ there is an $\epsilon>0$ such that the following holds.  The contact form $(1+\epsilon\pi^*H)\lambda$ has non-degenerate orbits upto action $T$ with simple Reeb orbits  $\gamma_{\ast}$, over the critical point $\ast$ of the function $H$. There is a choice of cylindrical almost complex structure $J_\epsilon$ that has enough regularity for computing cylindrical contact homology and the only rigid contributions are from lifts of gradient trajectories of $H$.
